ger connected to 802-3-ethernet ''\", as if the Ethernet had gone. Before it makes the tun, the adapter writes /run/udev/rules.d/90-<adapter>.rules, which marks the name NM_UNMANAGED, and reloads udev's rules (ExcludeFromNetworkManager); NetworkManager waits for udev before it looks at a device, so it never takes the tun. Once per boot, as /run is emptied at boot; a failure is a warning, since the VPN works the same without the rule; skipped where udev does not run. Tested on Lubuntu 26.04 (LXQt, nm-tray) with this build of the adapter in the 9.1.867 prerelease, which differs from it in this file only: the tun unmanaged, no notice at connect or disconnect, DNS on the tun, the public IP the server's, a reconnect reusing the rule; a tun made by hand without the rule still raised both notices. With its CHANGELOG line.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"commonfabric/labs","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:18:48Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"4d0cef54c4a3246f83984d288ece11cf8392afba","github_link":"https://github.com/commonfabric/labs/commit/4d0cef54c4a3246f83984d288ece11cf8392afba","commit_subject":"fix(piece): a pattern update may stop publishing an optional result field (#9554)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"GMOD/jbrowse-components","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:18:45Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"b1e0934fcf7f3945a65500e3db6de20041b477f1","github_link":"https://github.com/GMOD/jbrowse-components/commit/b1e0934fcf7f3945a65500e3db6de20041b477f1","commit_subject":"pggb_out_to_strain: the CFT073 allele's node id after the graph's rebuild","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"PrefectHQ/prefect","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-04T18:18:42Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"1d50f74d953cabd5ebed03f06d8e779d1c1fad19","github_link":"https://github.com/PrefectHQ/prefect/commit/1d50f74d953cabd5ebed03f06d8e779d1c1fad19","commit_subject":"Tolerate release of expired locks in MemoryLockManager and FileSystemLockManager (#23725)","ai_tool":"ZCode"},{"repo_name":"DataDog/integrations